{"severity":"error","file":"errors/division_by_zero_1.march","start_line":34,"start_col":18,"end_line":34,"end_col":25,"message":"division by `n` in `cap no_panic` module may be by zero — no refinement proves `n ≠ 0`.\n\n`n` is not a function parameter, so no refinement annotation reaches it. Guard the division instead, which the checker reads as proof: `if n == 0 do <fallback> else ... / n end`. Or use `Math.checked_div` or `Math.checked_mod`, which return `Option(Int)` instead of panicking.","code":"division_by_zero","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"REFINEMENT"}
